        "original_id": "dfdac1e8-3e0c-538d-828e-c471072dc5df",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Xawery Żuławski, Brian G. Hutton, Sonia Bohosiewicz, Dorota Masłowska\n- Films: Polish-Russian War, Where Eagles Dare, Kelly's Heroes, Rezerwat, Obława\n- Television series: Czas honoru\n- Places: Warsaw\n\nFacts:\n- Brian G. Hutton was born on January 1, 1935, and he was an American actor and film director.\n- Brian G. Hutton is most notable for directing the action films \"Where Eagles Dare\" in 1968 and \"Kelly's Heroes\" in 1970.\n- Xawery Żuławski was born on 22 December 1971 in Warsaw, and he is a Polish film director.\n- Polish-Russian War is a 2009 Polish film directed by Xawery Żuławski.\n- Polish-Russian War is based on the novel \"Polish-Russian War under the white-red flag\" by Dorota Masłowska.\n- Sonia Bohosiewicz has appeared in the films \"Rezerwat,\" \"Obława,\" and \"Polish-Russian War,\" and in the television series \"Czas honoru.\"\n- Brian G. Hutton died on August 19, 2014.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
